<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise 7.2 pct in week.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise 7.2 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 7.2 percent in the week to November 13 over the equivalent week a year ago, figures from the Bank of England showed. Last week the rise was 7.4 percent.</p>
<p>(figures in rounded billions of stg) -</p>
<p>			   Latest week  Previous week  Year-ago week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation   20.78	  20.78	     19.39</p>
<p> Bankers deposits	 2.04	   2.10		2.01</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
